+## Performance
+
+- The C routines behind `gsBound()`, `gsBound1()`, `gsProbability()`,
+  `gsDesign()` and `gsDensity()` were restructured without changing the
+  integration grid or the results (agreement with the previous
+  implementation to about 1e-16): the density update precomputes per-point
+  constants so its inner loop is one exponential per pair of grid points,
+  the lower-tail crossing probability in `gsBound1()` is evaluated once per
+  analysis instead of once per Newton iteration, and constant factors are
+  hoisted out of the boundary-search loops. Typical gains are 20% to 35%
+  for the core routines. Shared prototypes moved to `gsDesign.h`.
+
 ## Bug fixes
 
 - The Newton-Raphson boundary search in the C code no longer risks a `0/0`
